 "Two models answer the same two thousand test questions. Model A gets eighty percent right, model B eighty-three. Is B really better, or was it luck?": "bf396159e2.mp3",
 "Here are their first hundred answers, green for right and red for wrong. Both models find the same questions hard, but not always.": "dd2b669951.mp3",
 "The bootstrap: draw a new test set from this one, picking questions at random, some twice and some not at all. Measure B minus A. Do it four hundred times and pile up the answers.": "4aa8ae102f.mp3",
